## snp2.14
snp2.14:1.1 | S: So I have heard. | T: I have heard that
snp2.14:1.2 | S: At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. | T: on one occasion the Blessed One was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery.
snp2.14:1.3 | S: Then the lay follower Dhammika, together with five hundred lay followers, went up to the Buddha, bowed, sat down to one side, and addressed him in verse: | T: Then Dhammika the lay follower, together with 500 other lay followers, approached the Blessed One and, on arrival, having bowed down to him, sat to one side. As he was sitting there, he addressed the Blessed One in verses:
snp2.14:2.1 | S: “I ask you, Gotama, whose wisdom is vast: | T: “I ask you, Gotama, Deeply Discerning:
snp2.14:2.2 | S: what does one do to become a good disciple, | T: How-acting does one become a good disciple—
snp2.14:2.3 | S: both one who has left the home, | T: either one gone from home into homelessness,
snp2.14:2.4 | S: and the lay followers staying at home? | T: or a lay follower with a home?
snp2.14:3.1 | S: For you understand the course and destiny | T: For you discern the destination & future course
snp2.14:3.2 | S: of the world with all its gods. | T: of the world along with its devas
snp2.14:3.3 | S: There is no equal to you who sees the subtle meaning, | T: —there is no one equal to you in seeing the subtle goal;
snp2.14:3.4 | S: for you are the Buddha most excellent, they say. | T: for they call you foremost, awakened.
snp2.14:4.1 | S: Having experienced all knowledge, | T: Understanding all knowledge the whole Dhamma,
snp2.14:4.2 | S: you reveal the teaching out of sympathy for beings. | T: you proclaim it to beings with sympathetic mind.
snp2.14:4.3 | S: All-seer, you have cast off the veil, | T: Your roof opened up, All-around Eye,
snp2.14:4.4 | S: and immaculate, you dazzle the whole world. | T: you, stainless, illumine the whole world.
snp2.14:5.1 | S: The dragon king Erāvaṇa, <j>hearing you called ‘Victor’, | T: He came to your presence— Erāvaṇa, the nāga king,
snp2.14:5.2 | S: came into your presence. | T: having heard, ‘Conqueror.’
snp2.14:5.3 | S: He consulted with you then, <j>having heard your words, | T: Having consulted with you, having heard, he understood and,
snp2.14:5.4 | S: left consoled, saying ‘Excellent!’ | T: satisfied, (thought,) ‘Good.’
snp2.14:6.1 | S: And King Kuvera Vessavaṇa also | T: And King Vessavaṇa Kuvera
snp2.14:6.2 | S: approached to ask about the teaching. | T: came, inquiring about the Dhamma.
snp2.14:6.3 | S: You also answered him, O attentive one, | T: To him, too, you spoke when asked.
snp2.14:6.4 | S: and hearing you he too was consoled. | T: And he too, having heard, was satisfied.
snp2.14:7.1 | S: Those monastics of other religions given to debate, | T: And these sectarians, debaters by habit,
snp2.14:7.2 | S: whether Ājīvakas or Jains, | T: whether Ājīvakas or Nigaṇṭhas,
snp2.14:7.3 | S: all fail to overtake you in wisdom, | T: don’t overtake you in terms of discernment,
snp2.14:7.4 | S: like a standing man next to a sprinter. | T: as a person standing doesn’t catch up with one going quickly.
snp2.14:8.1 | S: Those brahmins given to debate, | T: And these brahmans, debaters by habit,
snp2.14:8.2 | S: some of whom are quite senior, | T: any elderly brahmans,
snp2.14:8.3 | S: all end up beholden to you for the meaning, | T: (none)
snp2.14:8.4 | S: and others too who think themselves debaters. | T: and any others who consider themselves debaters, all depend on you for the meaning.
snp2.14:9.1 | S: So subtle and pleasant is the teaching | T: For this Dhamma is subtle & blissful.
snp2.14:9.2 | S: that is well proclaimed by you, Blessed One. | T: This, Blessed One, well set-forth by you:
snp2.14:9.3 | S: It’s all we long to hear. So when asked, | T: We all want to hear it.
snp2.14:9.4 | S: O Best of Buddhas, tell us! | T: Tell it to us, Excellent Awakened, when asked.
