snp2.14:26.2 | S: or lie, or drink liquor. | T: tell a lie, nor be a drinker.
snp2.14:26.3 | S: Be chaste, refraining from sex, | T: One should abstain from uncelibate behavior— sexual intercourse—
snp2.14:26.4 | S: and don’t eat at night, the wrong time. | T: should not eat at night, a meal at the wrong time,
snp2.14:27.1 | S: Not wearing garlands or applying fragrance, | T: should not wear a garland or use scents,
snp2.14:27.2 | S: you should sleep on a low bed, <j>or a mat on the ground. | T: should sleep on a bed, on the ground, or on a mat,
snp2.14:27.3 | S: This is the eight-factored sabbath, they say, | T: For this, they say, is the eightfold uposatha,
snp2.14:27.4 | S: revealed by the Buddha, <j>who has gone to suffering’s end. | T: proclaimed by the Awakened One who has gone to the end of suffering & stress.
snp2.14:28.1 | S: Then having rightly undertaken the sabbath | T: Then, having kept, well-accomplished, the eightfold uposatha
snp2.14:28.2 | S: complete in all its eight factors | T: (none)
snp2.14:28.3 | S: on the fourteenth, fifteenth, <j>and eighth of the fortnight, | T: on the fourteenth, fifteenth, & eighth of the fortnight,
snp2.14:28.4 | S: as well as on the fortnightly special displays, | T: and on special days of the fortnight,
snp2.14:29.1 | S: at daybreak after the sabbath | T: (none)
snp2.14:29.2 | S: a clever person, rejoicing with confident heart, | T: with clear & confident mind, the observant person at dawn after the uposatha, confident, rejoicing,
snp2.14:29.3 | S: would distribute food and drink | T: should share food & drink,
snp2.14:29.4 | S: to the mendicant Saṅgha as is fitting. | T: as is proper, with the Saṅgha of monks.
snp2.14:30.1 | S: One should rightfully support one’s parents, | T: One should righteously support mother & father,
snp2.14:30.2 | S: and undertake a legitimate business. | T: should engage in righteous trade,
snp2.14:30.3 | S: A diligent layperson observing these duties | T: One heedful in this householder protocol
snp2.14:30.4 | S: ascends to the gods named ‘self-radiant’.” | T: goes to the devas called Self-radiant.”
snp2.14:30.5 | P: Dhammikasuttaṁ cuddasamaṁ. | T: (none)
snp2.14:30.6 | P: Cūḷavaggo dutiyo. | T: (none)
