## an7.53
an7.53:1.1 | S: So I have heard. | T: I have heard that
an7.53:1.2 | S: At one time the venerables Sāriputta and Mahāmoggallāna were wandering in the Southern Hills together with a large Saṅgha of mendicants. | T: on one occasion Ven. Sāriputta & Ven. Mahā Moggallāna were on a wandering tour of the Southern Mountains with a large Saṅgha of monks.
an7.53:1.3 | S: Now at that time the laywoman Veḷukaṇṭakī, Nanda’s mother, rose at the crack of dawn and recited the verses of “The Way to the Far Shore”. | T: And on that occasion, the female lay follower Veḷukaṇṭakin Nandamātar, having risen as night approached dawn, chanted the Pārāyana.
an7.53:2.1 | S: And at that time the great king Vessavaṇa was on his way from the north to the south on some business. | T: And on that occasion the great [deva] king Vessavaṇṇa was traveling from north to south on some business or other.
an7.53:2.2 | S: He heard Nanda’s Mother reciting, and stood waiting for her to finish. | T: He heard the female lay follower Nandamātar chanting the Pārāyana, and on hearing her, stood waiting for the end of her chant.
an7.53:3.1 | S: Then when her recital was over she fell silent. | T: Then the female lay follower Nandamātar, having chanted the Pārāyana, fell silent.
an7.53:3.2 | S: Then, knowing she had finished, Vessavaṇa applauded, saying, | T: Then the great king Vessavaṇṇa, knowing that her chant was ended, applauded her:
an7.53:3.3 | S: “Good, sister! Good, sister!” | T: “Excellent, sister! Excellent!”
an7.53:3.4 | S: “But who might you be, dearest?” | T: “But who’s there, O One of the Auspicious Face?”
an7.53:3.5 | S: “Sister, I am your brother Vessavaṇa, the great king.” | T: “I’m your brother, sister: the great king Vessavaṇṇa.”
an7.53:3.6 | S: “Good, dearest! Then may my recital of the teaching be my offering to you as my guest.” | T: “Excellent, O One of the Auspicious Face! Excellent! Then let this Dhamma sequence that I’ve chanted be your guest gift.”
an7.53:3.7 | S: “Good, sister! And let this also be your offering to me as your guest. | T: “Excellent, sister! And let this also be my guest gift.
an7.53:3.8 | S: Tomorrow, the mendicant Saṅgha headed by Sāriputta and Moggallāna will arrive at Veḷukaṇṭa before breakfast. When you’ve served the Saṅgha, please dedicate the religious donation to me. | T: This morning a Saṅgha of monks headed by Sāriputta & Moggallāna will be coming to Veḷukaṇṭaka before breakfast. Having served them, dedicate the offering to me.

